# Testing conventions

## File naming (required)

- **Always** use the `*.test.*` suffix for test files. Examples: `foo.test.ts`, `Bar.integration.test.tsx`, `jest.config.test.js`.
- **Never** add new `*.spec.*` files (`*.spec.ts`, `*.spec.tsx`, `*.spec.js`). The repo standardized on `*.test.*`; Vitest, Jest, and Sonar are configured for that pattern only.
- **Colocate** unit tests as a sibling of the module under test: `foo.ts` → `foo.test.ts` (use `.tsx` only if the test file contains JSX).
- **Do not** add new suites under `__TESTS__/`. Prefer TypeScript (`.test.ts` / `.test.tsx`) for new tests; existing `.test.js` is limited to legacy fixture/helpers (e.g. `libs/state/.../__FIXTURES__/`).

## Runner and stack

- **Client UI and libs pulled into client-web Vitest**: `yarn test` → `nx run client-web:test` → Vitest (jsdom) from [apps/client-web/vite.config.ts](apps/client-web/vite.config.ts). Use **Vitest** (`vi`, `describe`, …), not Jest, for these tests.
- **Server (`apps/server`)**: **Jest** (Node) via `yarn test:server` → `nx run server:test`. Test files: `apps/server/src/**/*.test.ts` (see [apps/server/jest.config.js](apps/server/jest.config.js)).
- **Shared packages with an Nx Jest target** (quota, repr-validation, repr-rules, constants): **Jest** via `nx run <project>:test`. Same `*.test.ts` naming; do not introduce `*.spec.ts`.
- **RTL**: `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/jest-dom` via [apps/client-web/src/setupTests.ts](apps/client-web/src/setupTests.ts). Legacy `jest.*` APIs are bridged to `vi` in that file.

## Integration tests (pages and `libs/components`)

- **Pages** (`apps/client-web/src/pages/<Page>/`): `integration-tests/**/*.test.tsx` (or `.test.ts` if no JSX).
- **`libs/components`** modules: `libs/components/src/<Component>/integration-tests/**/*.test.tsx`.
- **Harness**: render through [apps/client-web/src/test-utils/renderWithAppShell.tsx](apps/client-web/src/test-utils/renderWithAppShell.tsx) — Redux `Provider`, `MemoryRouter`, `CognitoAuthProvider`. Pass `preloadedState` and/or an existing `store` from [createTestStore.ts](apps/client-web/src/test-utils/createTestStore.ts) (no saga middleware).
- **Imports from `libs/**`into app test-utils**: prefer a **repo-relative** path into`apps/client-web/src/test-utils`where ESLint`import/no-relative-packages`applies;`@client-web/test-utils` exists in Vite for resolution when appropriate.
- **Components that import `store` from `@reprman/state/store`**: use `vi.mock('@reprman/state/store', async () => { … })` so the mock resolves before the component module; reuse the same store instance the `Provider` gets.

## Coverage requirements (required before merge)

Run **`yarn test:coverage`** from the repo root. CI and Sonar consume the merged LCOV at `apps/client-web/coverage/lcov.info` (paths must be repo-root-relative, e.g. `apps/server/src/handlers/billing/webhook.ts`, not `apps/client-web/coverage/src/...` — see [scripts/normalize-lcov-paths.mjs](scripts/normalize-lcov-paths.mjs)).

**Sonar vs local terminal reports:** Vitest/Jest print coverage against real source paths. Sonar only reads `lcov.info`. If path normalization is wrong, local thresholds can pass while Sonar shows **0% on new code**. After `yarn test:coverage`, spot-check: `grep '^SF:apps/server/src/' apps/client-web/coverage/lcov.info` should return hits.

| Source kind                                                   | Test style                                   | Per-file target (lines, branches, functions, statements) |
| ------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| Pure logic (`*.ts` / `*.js`, not UI)                          | Colocated unit tests, saga tests             | **100%**                                                 |
| `libs/shared/**`, `libs/utilities/**`, `*.{helpers,helper}.*` | Unit tests                                   | **100%**                                                 |
| UI (`*.tsx` / `*.jsx` pages and components)                   | Integration tests under `integration-tests/` | **≥ 80%**                                                |

- **New or changed production code** must meet the row above in the same PR. Sonar “new code” coverage follows the merged LCOV; untested handlers, sagas, and shared libs will fail the quality gate.
- **Do not** add coverage for excluded paths (below). Add tests for everything else you touch.

## Excluded from coverage (Vitest, Jest, Sonar)

Canonical list: [scripts/coverage-exclude-globs.mjs](scripts/coverage-exclude-globs.mjs) (wired into [apps/client-web/vite.config.ts](apps/client-web/vite.config.ts), [apps/server/jest.config.js](apps/server/jest.config.js), and [sonar-project.properties](sonar-project.properties)).

Excluded patterns include:

- **Test and harness code**: `**/*.test.*`, `**/*.integration.test.*`, `**/integration-tests/**`, `**/*.testData.ts`, `**/test-utils/**`, `**/__FIXTURES__/**`
- **Config / tooling**: `**/vite.config.ts`, `**/jest.config.js`, `**/jest.config.test.js`, `**/scripts/**`, `**/setupTests.ts`, `apps/server/esbuild.config.mjs`
- **Non-executable / barrel-only**: `**/*.types.ts`, `**/*.constants.ts`, `**/*.css`, `**/*.html`, thin `index.ts` re-export barrels (pages, components, modals, state, theme, types, etc.)
- **Server entry shim**: `apps/server/src/handlers/index.ts`

Interface-only `*.types.ts` files listed in the Vite coverage exclude are not thresholded.

## Mocks and timers

- **Do not remove or bypass** the global `vi.mock('@reprman/cognito-auth/configureAmplify', …)` in [setupTests.ts](apps/client-web/src/setupTests.ts). Avoid a blanket `vi.mock('@reprman/cognito-auth', importOriginal)` that re-exports the real barrel unless you also force `isCognitoConfigured: false`, or you will hit Amplify + `act` noise in jsdom.
- **`@testing-library/user-event` v13**: use `await userEvent.click(...)` (no `userEvent.setup()` unless the dependency is upgraded).
- **Fake timers**: `jest.useFakeTimers()` in tests is mapped to `vi` in setupTests; prefer `beforeAll`/`afterAll` and compute time-dependent values **inside** `it` blocks so timers apply after installation.

## Vitest discovery and coverage (monorepo)

- Test **include** and **coverage** live in [apps/client-web/vite.config.ts](apps/client-web/vite.config.ts). Lib tests are discovered via `**/*.test.{ts,tsx,js}` globs under `../../libs/...` (no `*.spec.*` patterns).
- **Sonar** test detection: [sonar-project.properties](sonar-project.properties) → `**/*.test.ts`, `**/*.test.tsx` only.
- Full merged coverage (Vitest + Jest, for CI/Sonar): `yarn test:coverage` → [scripts/run-all-coverage.mjs](scripts/run-all-coverage.mjs).
- Coverage uses **`allowExternal: true`** and **POSIX-style absolute `coverage.include` paths** so `libs/**` appears on Windows; if you change coverage layout, keep those constraints in mind.

## Commands

- Client-web Vitest (with coverage): `yarn test` (from repo root).
- Watch (no coverage): `yarn test:watch`.
- Server Jest: `yarn test:server`.
- Full monorepo coverage (Vitest + Jest → merged `lcov.info`): `yarn test:coverage`.
